# Testing Rule

## Test-First Mandate
Tests are written BEFORE full implementation (see `03-development.mdc`).
Tests define the contract; implementation fulfills the contract.

## AC Traceability — Required

Every test that implements an acceptance criterion MUST embed the AC ID in its description string. This is not optional.

**ID format:** `[TICKET-ID]-AC-N` (e.g., `PROJ-123-AC-1`)

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — AC ID embedded in description
it('[PROJ-123-AC-1] returns a token when credentials are valid', ...)
it('[PROJ-123-AC-2] throws UnauthorizedError when password is wrong', ...)

// ❌ WRONG — no AC reference
it('returns a token when credentials are valid', ...)
```

The same rule applies in all languages — put the AC ID in the test description/function name (see `agentic-pdlc-framework/agents/05-testing-agent.md` for per-language examples).

**Before writing tests:**
1. Load the requirements doc and extract all `[TICKET-ID]-AC-N` IDs
2. Build the AC → Test mapping table (in the requirements doc)
3. Every AC must map to at least one test

**After writing tests:**
- Update the Traceability Matrix in `docs/designs/TICKET-ID-requirements.md`
- Post the matrix as a Jira comment via `mcp__jira__add_comment`

## Test Structure

### Unit Tests
Test individual functions/methods in isolation.
```
Naming: [unit under test]_[scenario]_[expected outcome]
Example: login_withInvalidPassword_throwsUnauthorizedError
```

### Integration Tests
Test interactions between components (service + DB, API + service).
```
Naming: [flow description]_[scenario]_[expected outcome]
Example: userRegistration_withDuplicateEmail_returns409
```

### Test File Location
- Co-locate with source: `src/auth/auth.service.test.ts` next to `auth.service.ts`
- Or in `__tests__/` subdirectory matching source structure
- Follow project convention from `config/project.yaml`

## Test Coverage Requirements

| Category | Minimum Coverage |
|----------|-----------------|
| Business logic / domain | 90% |
| API handlers | 85% |
| Utility functions | 80% |
| UI components | 70% |
| Integration flows | Key paths covered |

## Test Quality Standards

### AAA Pattern — Required
Every test follows Arrange-Act-Assert:
```typescript
it('returns token when credentials are valid', async () => {
  // Arrange
  const user = createTestUser({ email: 'test@example.com' });
  mockUserRepo.findByEmail.mockResolvedValue(user);

  // Act
  const result = await authService.login('test@example.com', 'correct-password');

  // Assert
  expect(result.token).toBeDefined();
  expect(result.expiresIn).toBe(3600);
});
```

### Mock Discipline
- Mock external dependencies (DB, HTTP, file system, time)
- Do NOT mock internal business logic being tested
- Prefer integration tests with real DB over mocking the DB layer
- Always reset mocks between tests

### Test Data
- Use builder/factory functions for test data (`createTestUser()`, `buildOrder()`)
- Never use production data in tests
- Test boundary values: empty string, null, max length, negative numbers, zero

## What Must Be Tested

For every piece of implementation:
- [ ] Happy path — the expected, normal case
- [ ] Invalid input — wrong types, missing required fields, out-of-range values
- [ ] Error cases — external service failure, DB error, network timeout
- [ ] Edge cases — empty collections, single items, maximum limits
- [ ] Security cases — unauthorized access, injection attempts (for API/handlers)

## Running Tests

Use the command from `config/project.yaml` at `commands.test`.
Default fallbacks:
- JS/TS: `npm test` or `npx vitest run`
- Python: `pytest`
- Java: `mvn test` or `gradle test`
- Go: `go test ./...`

After implementation, ALL tests must pass. Never commit with failing tests.

## Test Reporting
After running tests, always include the AC Traceability Report:
```
Tests: 42 passed, 0 failed, 3 skipped
Coverage: 87% (lines), 82% (branches)
Duration: 4.2s

AC Traceability:
  PROJ-123-AC-1  ✅  2 tests passing
  PROJ-123-AC-2  ✅  1 test passing
  PROJ-123-AC-3  ❌  NO TEST — add before PR
```

If any AC shows ❌, block progress and write the missing tests before reporting done.
